YASDs come and go with everyone of us but from time to time one gets a
very full-flavored one, with a very pronounced *S*, a pure 99% YASD noir
infini, so to speak. This one was in a single night in the beginning of
September, still on 3.4.1.

Full-flavored, because it's an astral YASD and thus includes the entire
depth of the game as a background. Though the entry is a pure, ascetic
plunge (aided by a few trapdoors) to level 10 or so, without much of any
side-ways of gnomish or Japanese storekeeper's character.

Thus, glimz the elven witch set foot in a hall with two statues of
former heroes from the Fishpool domain (a part of the great Fi empire).
Among them she saw a whole gang of fierce, hissing cockatrices of which
vile creatures her grandfather had told her once. It is because of him
that the corpse of a lizard was kept at the bottom of her knapsack.

And, while she never needed it, she could comfortably rummage in the
statues' contents. She was way too unexperienced for the depths she had
reached, but clinging to these statues, hoped for salvation.

Among the belongings of the old rogue and the valkyrie she discovered a
gray stone that seemed to charm the gods. She also dug out a grayish
mail of what seemed to be huge reptile scales which did not interfere
with her elven witchcraft like the otherwise quite nice armor her
brethren crafted. Not a lesser gift was the good collection of
spell-books from the rogue. Other heroes must have fallen here, she
concluded; it was really an enormous amount of loot.

This all was not entirely to her liking because she had placed a few
conducts on herself which now seemed devalued. She had sworn not to
genocide or polymorph anybody or anything because she believed in the
true nature of things. She also forbade herself to wish for things,
artifact or not, for she feared to disturb the chaotic universe of her
gods. Nevertheless she went on, for she was the first wizard incarnation
of her soul (which existed in the mysterious world of Efil Laer when not
living in the real world).

After an amount of time spent avoiding the tougher creatures on that
level, securing the loot and eventually cleaning everything up, she went
deeper for the Amulet.

One thing she lacked was a decent weapon. Her god remained inexorable
and not even Magicbane, the first gift promised to the faithful of her
folk, appeared at her feet.

But she was soon crowned and she grew self-assured. With that Finger
clearing the way, Identify to support her knowledge of earthly things,
and the memories of that nurse dance to keep her mind and body fresh and
strong, unstoppable she seemed as well! Only named demons provided some
irritation, for she lacked physical power, but she did not let this
trouble her then.

In the Sanctum she was in record time as she had not strayed. There
Rodney bothered but went to the High Priest to steal the Precious. Soon
glimz met them and slew them with a single ray of pure energy.

The journey back began and it was an easy one: Rodney appears a fair
number of times, sparks fly from glimz' fingertips, self-assurance
grows. Time for the first mistake.

She was with the Amulet as she entered Sokoban and cursed-genocided
wraiths, greedy for new titles by which other demigods were to call her.
Now not only did she expend these valuable scrolls in this foolish
manner! She ate all corpses immediately on that spot, despite of her
perfect control over all spells she deemed necessary or even useful.
None of the more desirable ways of doing this title business crossed her
mind (or that of any of the consumed wraiths for she was still with her
trusty helm of telepathy).

After finishing this, she went further up and entered the Mines. What
for, one might ask again, but glimz was just beginning to have fun.
Doing everything in the opposite order, she entered Mines Town with the
Amulet.

Chaotic she is, shopkeepers fall, though one is spared as was an
emergency scroll of genocide from before. And then cockatrices appeared
from nowhere, the one spared was stoned and taken in a bag of holding!

glimz did not nest bags of holding and decided to keep her conducts and
thus a burdened elf, without speed boots or a good weapon left the earth
after writing her last book, called Stone to Flesh.

Rodney paid his due visit, elements of all sorts emerged to slay our
heroine, but she fights them with ease and unheeding her weaknesses
enters the astral plane and promptly proceeds to mistake two and final.

All monsters are detected, Famine is chosen, HoOA is ready. Glimz enters
and gets shrinked in a few turns, unable to cure her stunnedness,
HP-loss, and hunger while fighting burdened and not very fast.

Everything was so easy up to this point that she completely forgot to
devise any strategy for astral and that left an unpleasant after-taste!

